# =====================================================
# Docker ignore - excludes Windows-specific build artifacts
# =====================================================
# WHY THIS FILE MATTERS:
# Without .dockerignore, `COPY . .` in Dockerfile copies obj/ and bin/
# folders which contain Windows-only paths like:
#   'C:\Program Files (x86)\Microsoft Visual Studio\Shared\NuGetPackages'
# This crashes `dotnet publish` in the Linux container.
#
# Rule of thumb: Docker should only receive SOURCE code, not build artifacts.
# The container does its own `dotnet restore` and `dotnet publish` cleanly.
# =====================================================

# Build outputs (Windows-specific paths inside)
**/bin/
**/obj/

# Visual Studio
.vs/
*.suo
*.user
*.userosscache
*.sln.docstates
*.opendb

# Rider / VS Code
.idea/
.vscode/

# NuGet
**/packages/
*.nupkg
*.snupkg

# Test results
[Tt]est[Rr]esult*/
[Cc]overage*/

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Git
.git/
.gitignore
.gitattributes

# GitHub
.github/

# Docker
Dockerfile
docker-compose*.yml
.dockerignore

# Docs / infrastructure (don't need in image)
README.md
LICENSE
*.md
.azure/
